ble` den kept down to 0.35 holds it embattled for as long as it presses, its level easing toward 0.35, while a `modest` den kept down to 0.15 lets a town with a low ramp of its own (T₀ below about 0.18) go after the dwell (EXECUTED, `cure/D-ST-r3-probe/latchExit.out`) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-8 (the composer is MN's; ST registers) · RULINGS-ROUND2b (L-ST item 4's "never below the latch's floor" STRUCK)] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — SEAMS-r2-7 (ST's mirror of MN5's "may fall out", which the MN verifier executed false for a raid) · MN-V6 (A.3: the composer is a shared car) · note 3 (cite, never restate)]. The latch also tells what each hazard IS: only an untied FORTIFICATION at hand (a `capable` gang or stronger in a sound keep) crosses `ENTER_THRESHOLD` alone; every other untied kind's feeder is a TIPPER AND A SUSTAINER — it latches a town already pressed by crime, exhaustion or a neighbour's war (`T₀ + p·(1 − T₀) > 0.55`), keeps an embattled town embattled, and otherwise moves no danger consumer — while its OTHER arms fire regardless of the latch: the gate rows and the counterforce on every attached town by its distance band, the readiness membership on the AT-HAND towns only (ST9 governs) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — note 7: round 2 said the membership fired "on every attached town at every band"]; its felt lines say only what those arms did (§14) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — ST-r2-9: the landed step latches a calm record only "`if (rawT > T.ENTER_THRESHOLD)`"; each kind tabled in `cure/D-ST-r2-probe/scaleAndLatch.out`]. [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — the brief's "danger on the roads under it lowered within bounds" made exact: the only lowering is on what dens, menaces and roosts added; patrols (THE PATROLS, `briefs/L-PR.md` item 5) subtract on the same term.]
